  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In a closed tube whose length can be altered by sliding one of the halves relative to other is shown in the figure. In the initial condition the&nbsp;detector detects minimum&nbsp;intensity. One of the tubes&nbsp;is then displaced by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, during this displacement detector detects maximum intensity for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math>&nbsp;times and then a minimum intensity when the displacement is complete. What is the wavelength of sound?</p>\r\r<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0080_329af6927c60.jpg\" /></p>\r"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>10/9&#160;cm</mtext></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>1&nbsp;cm</mtext></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Path difference introduced due to displacement of tube is given by<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>2x=10&nbsp;cm</mtext></math><br />Now&nbsp;due to one wavelength change, maxima/minima will be attained once hence for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math>&nbsp;maxima's</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0080_329af6927c60.jpg\" style=\"width: 124px; height: 161px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>ΔP=10λ=10&nbsp;cm&nbsp;</mtext></math><br />So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>&nbsp;λ=1&nbsp;cm&nbsp;</mtext></math></p>"
  }
